{
  "_about": "How each exercise progresses, and so whether 0 kg means a missing load and whether an e1RM may be computed. Only `load` treats 0 kg / None as a missing load and allows an e1RM (the supports_load_estimate exclusions still apply on top). Separate from exercise-map.json (which maps muscles). `overrides` is a list of groups, one per (mode, why): every exercise in a group shares that mode and reason.",
  "_reviewed_on": "2026-10-17",
  "_how_lookup_works": "lifter override (profile) > exercise override > name prefix > category. Every catalog category has an entry; there is no fallback. Overrides are keyed 'CATEGORY:NAME' and exist only where a variant differs from what it would otherwise resolve to.",
  "modes": {
    "load": "Load first: keep the reps, add weight when the next step fits (reps only when one step is too big; see progression.md). Timed load sets (carries, weighted planks) keep the duration and add load. 0 kg = load missing.",
    "reps": "Add reps up to a ceiling, then a harder variation or a switch to load. 0 kg = no added load, a complete set. No e1RM.",
    "hold": "Add seconds up to a ceiling, then a harder variation or load. Timed sets are never hard sets. 0 kg = no added load. No e1RM.",
    "none": "Maintain; the Coach may plan it and next time is 'as last time' (dead bugs, mobility, warm-ups, conditioning, cardio). 0 kg = no added load. No e1RM."
  },
